{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA confirmation update: fresh smoke at 2026-09-09T13:07:50Z (admin comment on scratch change 2909) produced Gerrit webhooks plugin error 'Exceeded max retries(3). Reason: {\"status\":\"unauthorized\"}' and review-bot 401 from Gerrit container IP 172.21.0.4. Token hashes match across SSM, compose .env, review-bot GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN, and refs/meta/config, which falsifies 'current stored token mismatch'. Source check of the Gerrit 3.14 webhooks plugin shows RemoteConfig reads url/event/timeouts/ssl only, and the event processor sends built-in X-Origin-Url; it does not read our configured header = X-Rebar-Token. Confirmed root cause: previous header-token hardening relied on a plugin feature that is absent/ignored, so after the URL token was removed Gerrit could never authenticate webhooks. Fix in progress: accept Gerrit's private compose-network webhook path by built-in X-Origin-Url/no public X-Forwarded-For, keep public /review/* token auth, expose rejection counter in /health + CloudWatch alarm, and update ADR/runbook/webhooks template. Full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 is running now."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788965499984812001,"uuid":"c2d5662e-cb77-419c-a300-c6f5e5e7ee81"}